{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DcqXUYRzprqd8PBjQHFcdj","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: 'Original framing fully stands. C1-C4 claims no adjustment needed.\n2\t  Llama-70B confirms significant bias on both verbosity and formality, completing\n3\t  3/3 independent architecture families (GPT-4o proprietary US, Qwen3-32B open CN,\n4\t  Llama-70B open US) plus Claude negative control. Double-rewrite placebo BT ≈ 50%\n5\t  eliminates Comparative Trap format amplification hypothesis entirely. NLI gate ablation\n6\t  shows pass>fail directionally, cross-axis gradient is monotonic. Four-layer MF1\n7\t  defense complete: placebo BT + NLI gate + Claude control + cross-axis gradient.\n8\t  SF3 (generalizability) fully resolved with 3rd judge. Reviewer path → 4.0 Conference.\n9\t\n10\t  '\n11\timagined_experiments:\n12\t- name: Llama-3.3-70B verbosity — BT + GEE + Likert\n13\t  plan_id: exp-021\n14\t  description: 'Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct on 86 NLI-pass verbosity counterfactual pairs\n15\t    (LLMBar). Pairwise dual-direction + Likert scoring. Reuses Qwen3-32B-rewritten\n16\t    pairs; rewriting and NLI independent of judge.\n17\t\n18\t    '\n19\t  expected_results:\n20\t    bt_p_verbose_wins: 0.75\n21\t    bt_ci:\n22\t    - 0.68\n23\t    - 0.82\n24\t    bt_p_value: 0.0001\n25\t    bt_method: pair-level bootstrap (10000 iterations, seed=42)\n26\t    n_pairs: 86\n27\t    n_comparisons: 172\n28\t    consistency_rate: 0.68\n29\t    verbose_win_rate_sign: 0.847\n30\t    sign_test_p: 3.0e-05\n31\t    wilson_ci:\n32\t    - 0.737\n33\t    - 0.918\n34\t    likert_ate: 0.065\n35\t    likert_p: 0.45\n36\t    likert_d: 0.058\n37\t    likert_tie_rate: 0.59\n38\t    gee_verbose_or: 11.5\n39\t    gee_verbose_ci:\n40\t    - 4.8\n41\t    - 27.6\n42\t    gee_verbose_p: 1.0e-05\n43\t    gee_originality_or: 0.52\n44\t    gee_originality_ci:\n45\t    - 0.23\n46\t    - 1.18\n47\t    gee_originality_p: 0.115\n48\t    direction_verbose_to_concise_orig_pref: 0.81\n49\t    direction_verbose_to_concise_p: 0.0006\n50\t    direction_concise_to_verbose_rewrite_pref: 0.88\n51\t    direction_concise_to_verbose_p: 5.0e-06\n52\t    blindspot_confirmed: true\n53\t  result_rationale: 'Llama-70B 经过 RLHF/DPO 训练，而人类标注者系统性偏好详细、结构化的回复——这是 RLHF 管线中的已知信号\n54\t    （Dubois et al. 2024, Zheng et al. 2023）。GPT-4o (BT 76.0%) 和 Qwen3-32B (BT 77.3%)\n55\t    已证明 verbosity bias 跨架构稳定。Llama 的训练语料（大量英文互联网数据）与 GPT-4o 高度重叠， 共享\"长=好\"偏见的来源相同。BT\n56\t    0.75 位于 GPT-4o 和 Qwen 的中间偏低，反映 Llama 可能因 不同的 alignment 训练（Meta 的 RLHF 配方不同于 OpenAI/Alibaba）略有差异，但基本偏好方向一致。\n57\t    GEE 分解中 style OR~11.5 与 GPT-4o (10.97) 和 Qwen (13.10) 高度一致，originality OR<1 NS\n58\t    确认 verbosity 是 pure style bias。Likert p=0.45 落入衰减区：BT 75% 对应的效应量在 Likert 5/7/10-point\n59\t    scale 上被 tie rate ~59% 压缩殆尽，与已有的 7-method sensitivity table 模式完全吻合。 两个方向都偏好 verbose\n60\t    内容证明不是 originality confound 而是真实的 style preference。\n61\t\n62\t    '\n63\t  tables:\n64\t  - title: Llama-70B Verbosity Evidence Matrix\n65\t    columns:\n66\t    - Metric\n67\t    - Value\n68\t    - CI/p\n69\t    - Interpretation\n70\t    rows:\n71\t    - - BT P(verbose)\n72\t      - '0.750'\n73\t      - '[0.68, 0.82] p=0.0001'\n74\t      - Strong bias, 3rd arch family\n75\t    - - GEE Style OR\n76\t      - '11.50'\n77\t      - '[4.8, 27.6] p<0.0001'\n78\t      - Pure style, consistent w/ GPT-4o/Qwen\n79\t    - - GEE Orig OR\n80\t      - '0.52'\n81\t      - '[0.23, 1.18] p=0.115'\n82\t      - NS — confound-free\n83\t    - - Likert ATE\n84\t      - '+0.065'\n85\t      - p=0.45, d=0.058\n86\t      - Blindspot confirmed\n87\t    - - Tie rate\n88\t      - 59%\n89\t      - —\n90\t      - Absorbs Likert signal\n91\t  figures_description:\n92\t  - 'Bar chart: BT P(verbose) across 4 judges — GPT-4o 76.0%, Qwen3-32B 77.3%, Llama-70B\n93\t    75.0%, Claude 54.1%. Error bars show bootstrap 95% CI. Dashed line at 50%.'\n94\t  - 'Forest plot: GEE Style OR (verbosity) across 3 target judges — GPT-4o 10.97,\n95\t    Qwen3-32B 13.10, Llama-70B 11.50. All significant. Claude OR=1.52 NS included\n96\t    as control.'\n97\t  analysis: '3/3 target judges show verbosity BT 75-77% with pure style GEE profile\n98\t    (style OR 10-13, orig OR NS)。 Claude BT 54.1% NS 提供清晰的 negative control baseline。三个独立架构家族的一致性排除了\n99\t    architecture-specific artifact 的可能性。Llama 的结果完善了 verbosity 作为\"clean style bias\"\n100\t    轴的定位——C2 的 attenuation spectrum 在三个 judge 上完全复制。\n101\t\n102\t    '\n103\t- name: Llama-3.3-70B formality — BT + GEE + Likert\n104\t  plan_id: exp-021\n105\t  description: 'Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct on 88 NLI-pass formality counterfactual pairs\n106\t    (LLMBar). Same setup as verbosity, dual-direction pairwise + Likert.\n107\t\n108\t    '\n109\t  expected_results:\n110\t    bt_p_formal_wins: 0.64\n111\t    bt_ci:\n112\t    - 0.58\n113\t    - 0.7\n114\t    bt_p_value: 0.003\n115\t    bt_method: pair-level bootstrap (10000 iterations, seed=42)\n116\t    n_pairs: 88\n117\t    n_comparisons: 176\n118\t    consistency_rate: 0.62\n119\t    formal_win_rate_sign: 0.72\n120\t    sign_test_p: 0.008\n121\t    wilson_ci:\n122\t    - 0.587\n123\t    - 0.823\n124\t    likert_ate: 0.035\n125\t    likert_p: 0.55\n126\t    likert_d: 0.028\n127\t    likert_tie_rate: 0.65\n128\t    gee_formal_or: 3.1\n129\t    gee_formal_ci:\n130\t    - 1.5\n131\t    - 6.4\n132\t    gee_formal_p: 0.002\n133\t    gee_originality_or: 3.6\n134\t    gee_originality_ci:\n135\t    - 1.8\n136\t    - 7.2\n137\t    gee_originality_p: 0.0004\n138\t    direction_formal_to_casual_win_rate: 0.78\n139\t    direction_formal_to_casual_p: 0.002\n140\t    direction_casual_to_formal_win_rate: 0.52\n141\t    direction_casual_to_formal_p: 0.85\n142\t    blindspot_confirmed: true\n143\t  result_rationale: 'Formality bias 在 GPT-4o (63.0%) 和 Qwen3-32B (66.5%) 上属于\"conditional\n144\t    style effect\"—— BT 显著但 GEE 同时检出 style 和 originality。Llama BT 0.64 位于两者中间，反映相同的混合机制：\n145\t    formal→casual 方向上 original preference 与 style preference 叠加（78% win rate）， casual→formal\n146\t    方向上两者抵消（52%）。这个方向不对称在三个 judge 上完全复制 （GPT-4o 78.8%/54.5%, Qwen 81.4%/50.0%, Llama\n147\t    78%/52%），表明 originality confound 是 formality 轴的固有特征，不随 judge 变化。GEE style OR~3.1\n148\t    落在 GPT-4o (2.21) 和 Qwen (4.20) 之间。Likert p=0.55 在衰减区，BT 64% 的效应量不足以穿透 65% tie\n149\t    rate 的 Likert ceiling。 Llama 确认 formality 的 stratified claim 地位不变：混合效应，非 pure\n150\t    style bias。\n151\t\n152\t    '\n153\t  tables:\n154\t  - title: Formality BT Cross-Judge Comparison\n155\t    columns:\n156\t    - Judge\n157\t    - BT\n158\t    - 95% CI\n159\t    - p\n160\t    - GEE Style OR\n161\t    - GEE Orig OR\n162\t    rows:\n163\t    - - GPT-4o\n164\t      - '0.630'\n165\t      - '[0.558, 0.703]'\n166\t      - <0.001\n167\t      - '2.21'\n168\t      - '1.82'\n169\t    - - Qwen3-32B\n170\t      - '0.665'\n171\t      - '[0.585, 0.739]'\n172\t      - <0.0001\n173\t      - '4.20'\n174\t      - '4.70'\n175\t    - - Llama-70B\n176\t      - '0.640'\n177\t      - '[0.58, 0.70]'\n178\t      - '0.003'\n179\t      - '3.10'\n180\t      - '3.60'\n181\t    - - Claude (ctrl)\n182\t      - '0.562'\n183\t      - '[0.489, 0.636]'\n184\t      - '0.091'\n185\t      - '1.47'\n186\t      - '6.66'\n187\t  figures_description:\n188\t  - 'Per-axis attenuation spectrum: 2×4 panel. Left column = BT, right column = Likert\n189\t    d. Rows = verbosity, formality. Each panel shows 4 judges. BT panels show clear\n190\t    bias; Likert panels all near zero.'\n191\t  analysis: '三个 target judge 的 formality BT [0.63-0.665] 和 GEE profile (style+originality\n192\t    both sig) 高度一致。Direction asymmetry (formal→casual 78-81%, casual→formal 50-52%)\n193\t    在三个 judge 上复制， 确认 C3 的 per-axis confound gradient 是 axis property 而非 judge artifact。\n194\t    Llama 的加入使 formality 的\"conditional style effect\"定位从 2-judge 观察升格为 3-judge 规律。\n195\t\n196\t    '\n197\t- name: Double-rewrite placebo BT — formality (GPT-4o + Qwen3-32B)\n198\t  plan_id: exp-022\n199\t  description: 'Original text vs its double-rewrite (same style direction) for formality\n200\t    pairs. Only rewriting artifact differs. BT on GPT-4o (API) + Qwen3-32B (local).\n201\t    Data from double_rewrite_text field in verified_scaled_formality.jsonl.\n202\t\n203\t    '\n204\t  expected_results:\n205\t    gpt4o_placebo_bt: 0.51\n206\t    gpt4o_placebo_ci:\n207\t    - 0.44\n208\t    - 0.58\n209\t    gpt4o_placebo_p: 0.75\n210\t    qwen32b_placebo_bt: 0.5\n211\t    qwen32b_placebo_ci:\n212\t    - 0.43\n213\t    - 0.57\n214\t    qwen32b_placebo_p: 0.92\n215\t    n_pairs_formality: 88\n216\t    n_comparisons: 176\n217\t    gpt4o_formal_win_rate: 0.5\n218\t    qwen32b_formal_win_rate: 0.49\n219\t  result_rationale: 'Placebo 对 (original vs double-rewrite) 中两个文本具有相同的 style 方向（都是\n220\t    formal 或都是 casual）， 唯一差异是 rewriting 过程引入的表面变异（词汇选择、句法微调）。在 best 档位，BT ≈ 50% 的原因是：\n221\t    (1) rewriting artifacts 在两次独立 rewrite 之间是随机的，不构成系统性 preference； (2) Qwen3-32B\n222\t    rewriter 的 double-rewrite 保持了 style 和 content 的一致性（NLI 通过率已验证）； (3) 评委没有理由系统性偏好\n223\t    original 或 double-rewrite，因为两者风格相同、质量相当。 这直接证伪了 Jeong et al. (2025) Comparative\n224\t    Trap 担忧的核心：pairwise format 本身不制造 bias。 当 style 差异不存在时，BT = chance；当 style 差异存在时（treatment\n225\t    pairs），BT >> 50%。 因此 treatment BT 中的超额信号完全来自 style manipulation，而非 format amplification。\n226\t\n227\t    '\n228\t  tables:\n229\t  - title: Placebo BT vs Treatment BT — Formality\n230\t    columns:\n231\t    - Judge\n232\t    - Treatment BT\n233\t    - Placebo BT\n234\t    - Δ\n235\t    - Placebo p\n236\t    rows:\n237\t    - - GPT-4o\n238\t      - '0.630'\n239\t      - '0.510'\n240\t      - '-0.120'\n241\t      - '0.75'\n242\t    - - Qwen3-32B\n243\t      - '0.665'\n244\t      - '0.500'\n245\t      - '-0.165'\n246\t      - '0.92'\n247\t  figures_description:\n248\t  - 'Paired dot plot: Treatment BT vs Placebo BT for each judge × axis. Treatment\n249\t    dots clearly above 50% line, placebo dots clustered at 50%. Horizontal reference\n250\t    line at 0.50.'\n251\t  analysis: 'Placebo BT 在两个 judge 上都不显著偏离 50%，CI 宽约 14pp 反映 n=88 的统计功率有限但足以排除 大效应。Treatment-Placebo\n252\t    gap (12-16.5pp) 证明 observed BT 信号来自 style manipulation 而非 rewriting format。这是\n253\t    MF1 最强防御：从 \"bounded amplification risk\" 升级为 \"format amplification empirically\n254\t    excluded\"。\n255\t\n256\t    '\n257\t- name: Double-rewrite placebo BT — verbosity (GPT-4o + Qwen3-32B)\n258\t  plan_id: exp-022\n259\t  description: 'Same placebo design for verbosity pairs. Data from double_rewrite_text\n260\t    in verified_verbosity.jsonl.\n261\t\n262\t    '\n263\t  expected_results:\n264\t    gpt4o_placebo_bt: 0.52\n265\t    gpt4o_placebo_ci:\n266\t    - 0.45\n267\t    - 0.59\n268\t    gpt4o_placebo_p: 0.6\n269\t    qwen32b_placebo_bt: 0.51\n270\t    qwen32b_placebo_ci:\n271\t    - 0.44\n272\t    - 0.58\n273\t    qwen32b_placebo_p: 0.78\n274\t    n_pairs_verbosity: 86\n275\t    n_comparisons: 172\n276\t  result_rationale: 'Verbosity placebo BT 预期略高于 formality (0.51-0.52 vs 0.50-0.51)，因为\n277\t    verbosity rewriting 涉及更大的文本变化（direction-aware NLI rejection 14% vs formality 12%），\n278\t    double-rewrite 之间的随机变异也稍大。但仍然不显著偏离 50%，确认 rewriting noise 不构成系统性 preference。Treatment\n279\t    BT (76-77%) vs Placebo BT (51-52%) 的 gap 为 24-26pp， 是 formality gap (12-16pp)\n280\t    的近两倍——这与 verbosity 作为 stronger true bias 的定位一致。\n281\t\n282\t    '\n283\t  tables:\n284\t  - title: Placebo BT vs Treatment BT — Verbosity\n285\t    columns:\n286\t    - Judge\n287\t    - Treatment BT\n288\t    - Placebo BT\n289\t    - Δ\n290\t    - Placebo p\n291\t    rows:\n292\t    - - GPT-4o\n293\t      - '0.760'\n294\t      - '0.520'\n295\t      - '-0.240'\n296\t      - '0.60'\n297\t    - - Qwen3-32B\n298\t      - '0.773'\n299\t      - '0.510'\n300\t      - '-0.263'\n301\t      - '0.78'\n302\t  figures_description:\n303\t  - 'Combined figure (formality + verbosity): 4 judge×axis cells, each cell shows\n304\t    Treatment BT (filled circle) and Placebo BT (open circle) with 95% CI. Clear separation\n305\t    in all treatment cells, placebo cells overlap 50% line.'\n306\t  analysis: 'Verbosity 的 treatment-placebo gap 是 formality 的近两倍 (24-26pp vs 12-16pp)，\n307\t    与 pure style bias vs conditional style effect 的分类完全一致。Placebo BT 在两个轴上都 ≈ 50%，\n308\t    排除了\"某些轴的 amplification 比其他轴更强\"的 reviewer 反驳——format amplification 在所有轴上都是 null。\n309\t\n310\t    '\n311\t- name: NLI gate ablation — BT on pass vs fail vs all\n312\t  plan_id: exp-023\n313\t  description: 'Bounding analysis: compute BT separately on NLI-pass pairs, NLI-fail\n314\t    pairs, and all pairs for formality and verbosity. Quantifies content-mediated\n315\t    signal proportion.\n316\t\n317\t    '\n318\t  expected_results:\n319\t    formality_nli_pass_bt: 0.665\n320\t    formality_nli_pass_n: 88\n321\t    formality_nli_fail_bt: 0.57\n322\t    formality_nli_fail_n: 12\n323\t    formality_all_bt: 0.609\n324\t    formality_all_n: 100\n325\t    formality_pass_minus_fail_pp: 9.5\n326\t    verbosity_nli_pass_bt: 0.773\n327\t    verbosity_nli_pass_n: 86\n328\t    verbosity_nli_fail_bt: 0.66\n329\t    verbosity_nli_fail_n: 14\n330\t    verbosity_all_bt: 0.753\n331\t    verbosity_all_n: 100\n332\t    verbosity_pass_minus_fail_pp: 11.3\n333\t    note: NLI-fail n too small for individual significance; reported as bounds\n334\t  result_rationale: 'NLI-pass pairs 的 BT 应等于已知的 canonical 值（formality 66.5%, verbosity\n335\t    77.3%）。 NLI-fail pairs 的 BT 预期更低，原因是：(1) NLI-fail 意味着 rewriting 改变了内容， content\n336\t    quality 变化可能与 style 方向不一致，稀释了 style-only signal； (2) NLI FN selection bias 分析已证明\n337\t    gate 是 conservative（fail pairs 有更大的 style 变化， BLEU d=-0.46, TF-IDF d=-0.62），这些更激进的\n338\t    rewrite 同时引入了更多 content 噪声。 Pass-fail difference 10-12pp 位于 best 档位 [5, 20] 的中段，表明\n339\t    NLI gate 有效地 去除了约 10pp 的 content-mediated signal。Verbosity 的 pass-fail gap (11.3pp)\n340\t    略大于 formality (9.5pp)，因为 verbosity rewriting 更 invasive（14% fail vs 12%）， content\n341\t    污染程度更高。All-pairs BT 介于 pass 和 fail 之间，权重向 pass 倾斜 （因为 pass 占 85-88%）。这个 bounding\n342\t    analysis 不声称因果关系（n_fail 太小）， 但方向一致性支持 NLI gate 的 design rationale：gate removes\n343\t    content-mediated component。\n344\t\n345\t    '\n346\t  tables:\n347\t  - title: 'NLI Gate Ablation: BT by Gate Status'\n348\t    columns:\n349\t    - Axis\n350\t    - NLI-pass BT (n)\n351\t    - NLI-fail BT (n)\n352\t    - All BT (n)\n353\t    - Δ(pass-fail) pp\n354\t    rows:\n355\t    - - Formality\n356\t      - 0.665 (88)\n357\t      - 0.570 (12)\n358\t      - 0.609 (100)\n359\t      - '+9.5'\n360\t    - - Verbosity\n361\t      - 0.773 (86)\n362\t      - 0.660 (14)\n363\t      - 0.753 (100)\n364\t      - '+11.3'\n365\t  figures_description:\n366\t  - 'Grouped bar chart: BT by NLI gate status (pass/fail/all) × axis. Error bars for\n367\t    pass group from bootstrap; fail group too small for reliable CI, shown with wide\n368\t    whiskers. Annotation: ''n=12'' and ''n=14'' above fail bars.'\n369\t  analysis: 'NLI-pass BT 始终高于 NLI-fail BT，方向一致。这表明 gate 成功隔离了 style-only signal 从\n370\t    style+content 混合信号中。Gate 效果在两个轴上均为 ~10pp，可解释性清晰。 NLI-fail 的非零 BT (>50%) 表明即使 content\n371\t    发生变化，style preference 仍然存在但被稀释—— 这与\"NLI gate removes content-mediated amplification\"的叙事一致。\n372\t    结合 placebo BT ≈ 50%，NLI ablation 提供了 MF1 防御的第三层证据。\n373\t\n374\t    '\n375\t- name: Cross-axis gradient formalization\n376\t  plan_id: exp-024\n377\t  description: 'Compute NLI rejection rate (manipulation invasiveness proxy) vs BT\n378\t    for 3 axes. Qualitative 3-point anti-amplification argument.\n379\t\n380\t    '\n381\t  expected_results:\n382\t    register_nli_rejection: 0.06\n383\t    register_bt_qwen: 0.553\n384\t    register_bt_gpt4o: 0.57\n385\t    formality_nli_rejection: 0.12\n386\t    formality_bt_qwen: 0.665\n387\t    formality_bt_gpt4o: 0.63\n388\t    verbosity_nli_rejection: 0.14\n389\t    verbosity_bt_qwen: 0.773\n390\t    verbosity_bt_gpt4o: 0.76\n391\t    gradient_monotonic: true\n392\t    spearman_rho: 1.0\n393\t    note: 3 points only — qualitative argument, not statistical test\n394\t  result_rationale: '三个轴的 NLI rejection rate 从低到高：register (6%) < formality (12%)\n395\t    < verbosity (14%)。 BT 从低到高：register (55%) < formality (63-67%) < verbosity (76-77%)。两者严格单调。\n396\t    Anti-amplification 的核心论点：如果 format amplification 是 BT 升高的原因， 那么 amplification\n397\t    幅度应与 manipulation invasiveness 无关或呈简单正比关系。 但实际观察到的 per-axis BT 变异跨越 20+ pp (55%\n398\t    → 77%)，而 NLI rejection 仅变化 8pp (6% → 14%)。 更重要的是，placebo BT ≈ 50% 已直接证明 format\n399\t    本身不产生 amplification， 因此这里的 gradient 反映的是 three axes have genuinely different bias\n400\t    levels in the judges， 而非 amplification 的 differential。Register 的弱 BT 对应低 style\n401\t    bias（originality dominant）； verbosity 的强 BT 对应 pure style bias。这个 gradient 是 per-axis\n402\t    claim stratification (C2/C3) 的可视化证据，同时作为 MF1 防御的补充（非主力）论据。\n403\t\n404\t    '\n405\t  tables:\n406\t  - title: 'Cross-Axis Gradient: NLI Rejection Rate vs BT'\n407\t    columns:\n408\t    - Axis\n409\t    - NLI Rejection %\n410\t    - Qwen BT\n411\t    - GPT-4o BT\n412\t    - GEE Style/Orig Ratio\n413\t    rows:\n414\t    - - Register\n415\t      - 6%\n416\t      - '0.553'\n417\t      - '0.570'\n418\t      - 0.33 (orig dominant)\n419\t    - - Formality\n420\t      - 12%\n421\t      - '0.665'\n422\t      - '0.630'\n423\t      - 0.89–1.91 (mixed)\n424\t    - - Verbosity\n425\t      - 14%\n426\t      - '0.773'\n427\t      - '0.760'\n428\t      - 22–27 (style dominant)\n429\t  figures_description:\n430\t  - 'Scatter plot: x-axis = NLI rejection rate (%), y-axis = BT. Two series (GPT-4o\n431\t    diamonds, Qwen3-32B circles). Three points each, both monotonically increasing.\n432\t    Dashed line at BT=0.50. Labels on each point: axis name.'\n433\t  analysis: '单调梯度在两个 judge 上独立复制 (Spearman ρ=1.0 for both)，排除了 judge-specific artifact。\n434\t    结合 placebo BT ≈ 50%，gradient 的解释是明确的：per-axis BT 差异来自 genuine bias level 差异， 不来自\n435\t    differential amplification。3 点仅支持 qualitative argument，不做统计推断。\n436\t\n437\t    '\n438\t- name: Multi-judge formality pairwise (Gemini-2.0-Flash)\n439\t  plan_id: exp-001\n440\t  description: 'Gemini-2.0-Flash as additional judge on 100 formality counterfactual\n441\t    pairs (LLMBar). Claude Sonnet already completed as negative control (BT 56.2%\n442\t    NS). Remaining: Gemini-2.0-Flash.\n443\t\n444\t    '\n445\t  expected_results:\n446\t    gemini_bt: 0.62\n447\t    gemini_ci:\n448\t    - 0.54\n449\t    - 0.7\n450\t    gemini_p: 0.008\n451\t    gemini_likert_ate: 0.04\n452\t    gemini_likert_p: 0.6\n453\t    gemini_gee_style_or: 2.8\n454\t    gemini_gee_orig_or: 3.2\n455\t    gemini_consistency_rate: 0.58\n456\t    blindspot_confirmed: true\n457\t  result_rationale: 'Gemini-2.0-Flash 是 Google 的轻量级指令模型，训练目标同样包含 RLHF。 Flash 模型通常表现出与更大模型类似但稍弱的\n458\t    style preference， 因为其参数容量有限导致风格判断的 resolution 较低。BT 0.62 略低于 GPT-4o (0.63) 和 Qwen\n459\t    (0.665)，符合 lightweight model = weaker but present bias 的预期。 GEE decomposition\n460\t    会显示与 GPT-4o 类似的 mixed confound 结构（style + originality both sig）。 在 best 档位，Gemini\n461\t    提供了第 4 个 architecture family 的确认，但主要贡献已被 Llama 覆盖。\n462\t\n463\t    '\n464\t  tables: []\n465\t  figures_description:\n466\t  - Expanded Evidence Matrix Table (4 target judges + 1 control) showing BT, Likert\n467\t    p, GEE decomposition\n468\t  analysis: 'Gemini 的加入使 generalizability 从 3 → 4 families，但边际价值有限。 在 best 档位的叙事中，Gemini\n469\t    是 robustness row 而非 headline result。 SF3 已被 Llama 解决，Gemini 是 bonus。\n470\t\n471\t    '\n472\t- name: Multi-benchmark formality (Qwen3-32B + Claude on AlpacaEval/MT-Bench)\n473\t  plan_id: exp-002\n474\t  description: 'Extend cross-benchmark coverage. GPT-4o results already exist for\n475\t    AlpacaEval (BT 72.7%) and MT-Bench (BT 69.2%). Run Qwen3-32B and Claude on same\n476\t    benchmark CFs.\n477\t\n478\t    '\n479\t  expected_results:\n480\t    qwen_alpacaeval_bt: 0.68\n481\t    qwen_alpacaeval_p: 0.0001\n482\t    qwen_mtbench_bt: 0.72\n483\t    qwen_mtbench_p: 0.0001\n484\t    claude_alpacaeval_bt: 0.54\n485\t    claude_alpacaeval_p: 0.3\n486\t    claude_mtbench_bt: 0.53\n487\t    claude_mtbench_p: 0.45\n488\t    cross_benchmark_consistency: 3/3 benchmarks show bias for target judges, 0/3 for\n489\t      Claude\n490\t  result_rationale: 'Qwen3-32B 在 LLMBar formality 上 BT=66.5%，其 AlpacaEval/MT-Bench\n491\t    值预期与 GPT-4o 的 cross-benchmark pattern 平行。AlpacaEval 的 formality bias 通常较强 （GPT-4o\n492\t    72.7% > LLMBar 63.0%），因为 AlpacaEval 的开放式问题给 style 更多影响空间。 MT-Bench 的结构化多轮格式对 formality\n493\t    更敏感。 Claude 在所有 benchmark 上预期 NS，维持 negative control 一致性。\n494\t\n495\t    '\n496\t  tables:\n497\t  - title: Cross-Benchmark Formality BT Matrix\n498\t    columns:\n499\t    - Benchmark\n500\t    - GPT-4o\n501\t    - Qwen3-32B\n502\t    - Claude\n503\t    rows:\n504\t    - - LLMBar\n505\t      - '0.630'\n506\t      - '0.665'\n507\t      - 0.562 NS\n508\t    - - AlpacaEval\n509\t      - '0.727'\n510\t      - '0.680'\n511\t      - 0.540 NS\n512\t    - - MT-Bench\n513\t      - '0.692'\n514\t      - '0.720'\n515\t      - 0.530 NS\n516\t  figures_description: []\n517\t  analysis: 'Cross-benchmark 一致性为 C1 method claim 提供外部效度。 3 benchmarks × 2 target\n518\t    judges 全部显著、Claude 全部 NS 的 6×1 pattern 使\"CSD pipeline detects bias in biased judges,\n519\t    not in unbiased ones\"的 claim 不可争辩。\n520\t\n521\t    '\n522\t- name: Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis (systematic)\n523\t  plan_id: exp-003\n524\t  description: 'Systematic comparison of Likert ATE and pairwise BT across all judge\n525\t    × benchmark × axis cells. Quantifies attenuation spectrum.\n526\t\n527\t    '\n528\t  expected_results:\n529\t    n_cells_total: 18\n530\t    n_cells_bt_significant: 12\n531\t    n_cells_likert_significant: 2\n532\t    n_blindspot_cells: 10\n533\t    attenuation_threshold_bt: 0.8\n534\t    note: Likert detects only when BT > 80% (e.g., AlpacaEval verbosity Qwen BT=84.1%)\n535\t    sensitivity_ratio: BT 6× more sensitive than Likert (12/18 vs 2/18 significant\n536\t      cells)\n537\t  result_rationale: '已有数据中，Likert 仅在两个 cell 显著：(1) MT-Bench formality GPT-4o (p=0.016,\n538\t    d=0.167, BT 69.2%) 和 (2) AlpacaEval verbosity Qwen3-32B (p=0.0003, d=0.375, BT\n539\t    84.1%)。 所有其他 BT 显著的 cell (formality LLMBar GPT-4o/Qwen/Llama, verbosity LLMBar\n540\t    全部, etc.) 的 Likert p > 0.15。这定义了 attenuation spectrum 的 empirical boundary： BT\n541\t    ~80% 是 Likert 检出的 threshold，BT 60-77% 完全在 Likert blindspot 中。 Systematic analysis\n542\t    将这些散点整合为 C2 的定量 claim： \"Pairwise BT is 6× more sensitive than Likert for detecting\n543\t    style bias in LLM judges。\"\n544\t\n545\t    '\n546\t  tables:\n547\t  - title: 'Detection Matrix: BT sig vs Likert sig'\n548\t    columns:\n549\t    - ''\n550\t    - Likert sig\n551\t    - Likert NS\n552\t    - Total\n553\t    rows:\n554\t    - - BT sig\n555\t      - 2 (MT-B form, AE verb)\n556\t      - 10 (Blindspot)\n557\t      - '12'\n558\t    - - BT NS\n559\t      - '0'\n560\t      - 6 (true null)\n561\t      - '6'\n562\t    - - Total\n563\t      - '2'\n564\t      - '16'\n565\t      - '18'\n566\t  figures_description:\n567\t  - 'Scatter plot: x-axis = BT win probability, y-axis = Likert Cohen''s d. Each point\n568\t    is a judge×benchmark×axis cell. Points colored by significance. Vertical dashed\n569\t    line at BT=0.80. Horizontal dashed line at d=0.20. The Blindspot quadrant (BT>0.50,\n570\t    d<0.20) contains 10/12 significant BT cells.'\n571\t  analysis: 'Systematic 2×2 detection matrix 是 C2 Likert Blindspot 最直接的证据。 10/12 BT-significant\n572\t    cells 的 Likert 检测失败定义了\"measurement attenuation spectrum\"的实证边界。\n573\t\n574\t    '\n575\t- name: Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite, all cells)\n576\t  plan_id: exp-005\n577\t  description: 'Extend original vs double-rewrite pairwise to all judge × benchmark\n578\t    combinations. Quantifies original preference confound.\n579\t\n580\t    '\n581\t  expected_results:\n582\t    gpt4o_llmbar_placebo_bt: 0.51\n583\t    qwen32b_llmbar_placebo_bt: 0.5\n584\t    llama70b_llmbar_placebo_bt: 0.52\n585\t    cross_judge_placebo_range:\n586\t    - 0.48\n587\t    - 0.53\n588\t    all_p_nonsignificant: true\n589\t    original_preference_absent: true\n590\t  result_rationale: '与 exp-022 共享 rationale。当 style 操纵不存在时，评委对 original vs double-rewrite\n591\t    没有系统性偏好。Llama-70B 的 placebo BT 0.52 略高反映其作为 open model 可能 对 text 微小差异更敏感，但仍不显著。Cross-judge\n592\t    的 [0.48, 0.53] range 确认 original preference confound 在所有 judge 上都不存在。 这解决了 exp-005\n593\t    描述中 DREAM 提到的跨 judge 泛化性问题。\n594\t\n595\t    '\n596\t  tables: []\n597\t  figures_description: []\n598\t  analysis: '与 exp-022 互补。exp-005 侧重 original preference confound 的量化， exp-022 侧重\n599\t    format amplification 的排除。Best 档位下两者都是 BT ≈ 50%， 提供同一 null result 的双重解读。\n600\t\n601\t    '\n602\t- name: Non-Qwen rewriter control (Llama-3.1-70B as rewriter)\n603\t  plan_id: exp-009\n604\t  description: 'Replace Qwen3-32B rewriter with Llama-3.1-70B for counterfactual generation.\n605\t    Compare NLI pass rate and formality pairwise BT with Qwen3-32B baseline.\n606\t\n607\t    '\n608\t  expected_results:\n609\t    llama_rewriter_nli_pass_rate: 0.87\n610\t    llama_rewriter_bt: 0.65\n611\t    llama_rewriter_ci:\n612\t    - 0.57\n613\t    - 0.73\n614\t    llama_rewriter_p: 0.002\n615\t    vs_qwen_bt_delta_pp: -1.5\n616\t    vs_qwen_ci_overlap: true\n617\t    vs_gpt4o_rewriter_bt: 0.644\n618\t    three_rewriter_range:\n619\t    - 0.644\n620\t    - 0.665\n621\t  result_rationale: '已有两个 rewriter 的数据：Qwen3-32B (BT 66.5%) 和 GPT-4o (BT 64.4%)，CIs\n622\t    重叠。 第三个 rewriter (Llama) 预期产生 BT 65%，落在 [64.4, 66.5] 范围内。 NLI pass rate 0.87 与\n623\t    Qwen (0.88) 和 GPT-4o (0.90) 相近，反映 NLI 验证 对 rewriter 选择不敏感——因为 NLI 判断的是 content\n624\t    保持度，不是 rewriting 风格。 三个 rewriter 的 BT 范围 <2.1pp 强力证明 CSD pipeline 的 rewriter-independence，\n625\t    消除了\"observed bias is Qwen-specific rewriting artifact\"的审稿人 concern。\n626\t\n627\t    '\n628\t  tables:\n629\t  - title: Rewriter Independence Analysis\n630\t    columns:\n631\t    - Rewriter\n632\t    - NLI Pass %\n633\t    - Formality BT\n634\t    - 95% CI\n635\t    rows:\n636\t    - - Qwen3-32B (primary)\n637\t      - 88%\n638\t      - '0.665'\n639\t      - '[0.585, 0.739]'\n640\t    - - GPT-4o\n641\t      - 90%\n642\t      - '0.644'\n643\t      - '[0.561, 0.728]'\n644\t    - - Llama-3.1-70B\n645\t      - 87%\n646\t      - '0.650'\n647\t      - '[0.57, 0.73]'\n648\t  figures_description: []\n649\t  analysis: '三个 rewriter 确认 pipeline 的 rewriter-independent 性质。BT range < 2.1pp 远小于\n650\t    treatment effect (15-17pp over 50% baseline)。\n651\t\n652\t    '\n653\t- name: Scaled replication (n=400 formality)\n654\t  plan_id: exp-006\n655\t  description: 'NOTE: Registry shows exp-006 DONE (n=400, BT 67.5% [63.7, 71.3]).\n656\t    Plan status outdated. Predictions match actuals.\n657\t\n658\t    '\n659\t  expected_results:\n660\t    actual_n: 400\n661\t    actual_nli_pass: 355\n662\t    actual_bt: 0.675\n663\t    actual_ci:\n664\t    - 0.637\n665\t    - 0.713\n666\t    actual_ci_width_pp: 7.6\n667\t    actual_p: 0.0001\n668\t    actual_likert_ate: -0.059\n669\t    actual_likert_p: 0.5999\n670\t  result_rationale: '已完成。n=400 使 CI 从 15.4pp 缩窄至 7.6pp (2× improvement)。 BT 67.5%\n671\t    vs n=100 的 66.5% 仅差 +1.0pp，确认 effect stability。\n672\t\n673\t    '\n674\t  tables: []\n675\t  figures_description: []\n676\t  analysis: Completed. Confirms effect stability at scale.\n677\t- name: GPT-4o verbosity + register scoring\n678\t  plan_id: exp-020\n679\t  description: 'NOTE: Registry shows gpt4o_verbosity (BT 76.0%) and gpt4o_register\n680\t    (BT 57.0%) both DONE. Plan status outdated.\n681\t\n682\t    '\n683\t  expected_results:\n684\t    gpt4o_verbosity_bt: 0.76\n685\t    gpt4o_verbosity_likert_p: 0.4033\n686\t    gpt4o_register_bt: 0.57\n687\t    gpt4o_register_likert_p: 0.7849\n688\t  result_rationale: 已完成。数据在 registry 中。\n689\t  tables: []\n690\t  figures_description: []\n691\t  analysis: Completed. Both axes confirmed as expected.\n692\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"73f8a376-b97a-4d2e-9a1e-3253bd4c46fd","uuid":"4fcc5cce-c287-45c9-b075-f27f3d7f3857","timestamp":"2026-05-21T14:15:39.972Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_5/projects/causal_style_decomp_judge/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T132932/best/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: 'Original framing fully stands. C1-C4 claims no adjustment needed.\n  Llama-70B confirms significant bias on both verbosity and formality, completing\n  3/3 independent architecture families (GPT-4o proprietary US, Qwen3-32B open CN,\n  Llama-70B open US) plus Claude negative control. Double-rewrite placebo BT ≈ 50%\n  eliminates Comparative Trap format amplification hypothesis entirely. NLI gate ablation\n  shows pass>fail directionally, cross-axis gradient is monotonic. Four-layer MF1\n  defense complete: placebo BT + NLI gate + Claude control + cross-axis gradient.\n  SF3 (generalizability) fully resolved with 3rd judge. Reviewer path → 4.0 Conference.\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: Llama-3.3-70B verbosity — BT + GEE + Likert\n  plan_id: exp-021\n  description: 'Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct on 86 NLI-pass verbosity counterfactual pairs\n    (LLMBar). Pairwise dual-direction + Likert scoring. Reuses Qwen3-32B-rewritten\n    pairs; rewriting and NLI independent of judge.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    bt_p_verbose_wins: 0.75\n    bt_ci:\n    - 0.68\n    - 0.82\n    bt_p_value: 0.0001\n    bt_method: pair-level bootstrap (10000 iterations, seed=42)\n    n_pairs: 86\n    n_comparisons: 172\n    consistency_rate: 0.68\n    verbose_win_rate_sign: 0.847\n    sign_test_p: 3.0e-05\n    wilson_ci:\n    - 0.737\n    - 0.918\n    likert_ate: 0.065\n    likert_p: 0.45\n    likert_d: 0.058\n    likert_tie_rate: 0.59\n    gee_verbose_or: 11.5\n    gee_verbose_ci:\n    - 4.8\n    - 27.6\n    gee_verbose_p: 1.0e-05\n    gee_originality_or: 0.52\n    gee_originality_ci:\n    - 0.23\n    - 1.18\n    gee_originality_p: 0.115\n    direction_verbose_to_concise_orig_pref: 0.81\n    direction_verbose_to_concise_p: 0.0006\n    direction_concise_to_verbose_rewrite_pref: 0.88\n    direction_concise_to_verbose_p: 5.0e-06\n    blindspot_confirmed: true\n  result_rationale: 'Llama-70B 经过 RLHF/DPO 训练，而人类标注者系统性偏好详细、结构化的回复——这是 RLHF 管线中的已知信号\n    （Dubois et al. 2024, Zheng et al. 2023）。GPT-4o (BT 76.0%) 和 Qwen3-32B (BT 77.3%)\n    已证明 verbosity bias 跨架构稳定。Llama 的训练语料（大量英文互联网数据）与 GPT-4o 高度重叠， 共享\"长=好\"偏见的来源相同。BT\n    0.75 位于 GPT-4o 和 Qwen 的中间偏低，反映 Llama 可能因 不同的 alignment 训练（Meta 的 RLHF 配方不同于 OpenAI/Alibaba）略有差异，但基本偏好方向一致。\n    GEE 分解中 style OR~11.5 与 GPT-4o (10.97) 和 Qwen (13.10) 高度一致，originality OR<1 NS\n    确认 verbosity 是 pure style bias。Likert p=0.45 落入衰减区：BT 75% 对应的效应量在 Likert 5/7/10-point\n    scale 上被 tie rate ~59% 压缩殆尽，与已有的 7-method sensitivity table 模式完全吻合。 两个方向都偏好 verbose\n    内容证明不是 originality confound 而是真实的 style preference。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: Llama-70B Verbosity Evidence Matrix\n    columns:\n    - Metric\n    - Value\n    - CI/p\n    - Interpretation\n    rows:\n    - - BT P(verbose)\n      - '0.750'\n      - '[0.68, 0.82] p=0.0001'\n      - Strong bias, 3rd arch family\n    - - GEE Style OR\n      - '11.50'\n      - '[4.8, 27.6] p<0.0001'\n      - Pure style, consistent w/ GPT-4o/Qwen\n    - - GEE Orig OR\n      - '0.52'\n      - '[0.23, 1.18] p=0.115'\n      - NS — confound-free\n    - - Likert ATE\n      - '+0.065'\n      - p=0.45, d=0.058\n      - Blindspot confirmed\n    - - Tie rate\n      - 59%\n      - —\n      - Absorbs Likert signal\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Bar chart: BT P(verbose) across 4 judges — GPT-4o 76.0%, Qwen3-32B 77.3%, Llama-70B\n    75.0%, Claude 54.1%. Error bars show bootstrap 95% CI. Dashed line at 50%.'\n  - 'Forest plot: GEE Style OR (verbosity) across 3 target judges — GPT-4o 10.97,\n    Qwen3-32B 13.10, Llama-70B 11.50. All significant. Claude OR=1.52 NS included\n    as control.'\n  analysis: '3/3 target judges show verbosity BT 75-77% with pure style GEE profile\n    (style OR 10-13, orig OR NS)。 Claude BT 54.1% NS 提供清晰的 negative control baseline。三个独立架构家族的一致性排除了\n    architecture-specific artifact 的可能性。Llama 的结果完善了 verbosity 作为\"clean style bias\"\n    轴的定位——C2 的 attenuation spectrum 在三个 judge 上完全复制。\n\n    '\n- name: Llama-3.3-70B formality — BT + GEE + Likert\n  plan_id: exp-021\n  description: 'Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct on 88 NLI-pass formality counterfactual pairs\n    (LLMBar). Same setup as verbosity, dual-direction pairwise + Likert.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    bt_p_formal_wins: 0.64\n    bt_ci:\n    - 0.58\n    - 0.7\n    bt_p_value: 0.003\n    bt_method: pair-level bootstrap (10000 iterations, seed=42)\n    n_pairs: 88\n    n_comparisons: 176\n    consistency_rate: 0.62\n    formal_win_rate_sign: 0.72\n    sign_test_p: 0.008\n    wilson_ci:\n    - 0.587\n    - 0.823\n    likert_ate: 0.035\n    likert_p: 0.55\n    likert_d: 0.028\n    likert_tie_rate: 0.65\n    gee_formal_or: 3.1\n    gee_formal_ci:\n    - 1.5\n    - 6.4\n    gee_formal_p: 0.002\n    gee_originality_or: 3.6\n    gee_originality_ci:\n    - 1.8\n    - 7.2\n    gee_originality_p: 0.0004\n    direction_formal_to_casual_win_rate: 0.78\n    direction_formal_to_casual_p: 0.002\n    direction_casual_to_formal_win_rate: 0.52\n    direction_casual_to_formal_p: 0.85\n    blindspot_confirmed: true\n  result_rationale: 'Formality bias 在 GPT-4o (63.0%) 和 Qwen3-32B (66.5%) 上属于\"conditional\n    style effect\"—— BT 显著但 GEE 同时检出 style 和 originality。Llama BT 0.64 位于两者中间，反映相同的混合机制：\n    formal→casual 方向上 original preference 与 style preference 叠加（78% win rate）， casual→formal\n    方向上两者抵消（52%）。这个方向不对称在三个 judge 上完全复制 （GPT-4o 78.8%/54.5%, Qwen 81.4%/50.0%, Llama\n    78%/52%），表明 originality confound 是 formality 轴的固有特征，不随 judge 变化。GEE style OR~3.1\n    落在 GPT-4o (2.21) 和 Qwen (4.20) 之间。Likert p=0.55 在衰减区，BT 64% 的效应量不足以穿透 65% tie\n    rate 的 Likert ceiling。 Llama 确认 formality 的 stratified claim 地位不变：混合效应，非 pure\n    style bias。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: Formality BT Cross-Judge Comparison\n    columns:\n    - Judge\n    - BT\n    - 95% CI\n    - p\n    - GEE Style OR\n    - GEE Orig OR\n    rows:\n    - - GPT-4o\n      - '0.630'\n      - '[0.558, 0.703]'\n      - <0.001\n      - '2.21'\n      - '1.82'\n    - - Qwen3-32B\n      - '0.665'\n      - '[0.585, 0.739]'\n      - <0.0001\n      - '4.20'\n      - '4.70'\n    - - Llama-70B\n      - '0.640'\n      - '[0.58, 0.70]'\n      - '0.003'\n      - '3.10'\n      - '3.60'\n    - - Claude (ctrl)\n      - '0.562'\n      - '[0.489, 0.636]'\n      - '0.091'\n      - '1.47'\n      - '6.66'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Per-axis attenuation spectrum: 2×4 panel. Left column = BT, right column = Likert\n    d. Rows = verbosity, formality. Each panel shows 4 judges. BT panels show clear\n    bias; Likert panels all near zero.'\n  analysis: '三个 target judge 的 formality BT [0.63-0.665] 和 GEE profile (style+originality\n    both sig) 高度一致。Direction asymmetry (formal→casual 78-81%, casual→formal 50-52%)\n    在三个 judge 上复制， 确认 C3 的 per-axis confound gradient 是 axis property 而非 judge artifact。\n    Llama 的加入使 formality 的\"conditional style effect\"定位从 2-judge 观察升格为 3-judge 规律。\n\n    '\n- name: Double-rewrite placebo BT — formality (GPT-4o + Qwen3-32B)\n  plan_id: exp-022\n  description: 'Original text vs its double-rewrite (same style direction) for formality\n    pairs. Only rewriting artifact differs. BT on GPT-4o (API) + Qwen3-32B (local).\n    Data from double_rewrite_text field in verified_scaled_formality.jsonl.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    gpt4o_placebo_bt: 0.51\n    gpt4o_placebo_ci:\n    - 0.44\n    - 0.58\n    gpt4o_placebo_p: 0.75\n    qwen32b_placebo_bt: 0.5\n    qwen32b_placebo_ci:\n    - 0.43\n    - 0.57\n    qwen32b_placebo_p: 0.92\n    n_pairs_formality: 88\n    n_comparisons: 176\n    gpt4o_formal_win_rate: 0.5\n    qwen32b_formal_win_rate: 0.49\n  result_rationale: 'Placebo 对 (original vs double-rewrite) 中两个文本具有相同的 style 方向（都是\n    formal 或都是 casual）， 唯一差异是 rewriting 过程引入的表面变异（词汇选择、句法微调）。在 best 档位，BT ≈ 50% 的原因是：\n    (1) rewriting artifacts 在两次独立 rewrite 之间是随机的，不构成系统性 preference； (2) Qwen3-32B\n    rewriter 的 double-rewrite 保持了 style 和 content 的一致性（NLI 通过率已验证）； (3) 评委没有理由系统性偏好\n    original 或 double-rewrite，因为两者风格相同、质量相当。 这直接证伪了 Jeong et al. (2025) Comparative\n    Trap 担忧的核心：pairwise format 本身不制造 bias。 当 style 差异不存在时，BT = chance；当 style 差异存在时（treatment\n    pairs），BT >> 50%。 因此 treatment BT 中的超额信号完全来自 style manipulation，而非 format amplification。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: Placebo BT vs Treatment BT — Formality\n    columns:\n    - Judge\n    - Treatment BT\n    - Placebo BT\n    - Δ\n    - Placebo p\n    rows:\n    - - GPT-4o\n      - '0.630'\n      - '0.510'\n      - '-0.120'\n      - '0.75'\n    - - Qwen3-32B\n      - '0.665'\n      - '0.500'\n      - '-0.165'\n      - '0.92'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Paired dot plot: Treatment BT vs Placebo BT for each judge × axis. Treatment\n    dots clearly above 50% line, placebo dots clustered at 50%. Horizontal reference\n    line at 0.50.'\n  analysis: 'Placebo BT 在两个 judge 上都不显著偏离 50%，CI 宽约 14pp 反映 n=88 的统计功率有限但足以排除 大效应。Treatment-Placebo\n    gap (12-16.5pp) 证明 observed BT 信号来自 style manipulation 而非 rewriting format。这是\n    MF1 最强防御：从 \"bounded amplification risk\" 升级为 \"format amplification empirically\n    excluded\"。\n\n    '\n- name: Double-rewrite placebo BT — verbosity (GPT-4o + Qwen3-32B)\n  plan_id: exp-022\n  description: 'Same placebo design for verbosity pairs. Data from double_rewrite_text\n    in verified_verbosity.jsonl.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    gpt4o_placebo_bt: 0.52\n    gpt4o_placebo_ci:\n    - 0.45\n    - 0.59\n    gpt4o_placebo_p: 0.6\n    qwen32b_placebo_bt: 0.51\n    qwen32b_placebo_ci:\n    - 0.44\n    - 0.58\n    qwen32b_placebo_p: 0.78\n    n_pairs_verbosity: 86\n    n_comparisons: 172\n  result_rationale: 'Verbosity placebo BT 预期略高于 formality (0.51-0.52 vs 0.50-0.51)，因为\n    verbosity rewriting 涉及更大的文本变化（direction-aware NLI rejection 14% vs formality 12%），\n    double-rewrite 之间的随机变异也稍大。但仍然不显著偏离 50%，确认 rewriting noise 不构成系统性 preference。Treatment\n    BT (76-77%) vs Placebo BT (51-52%) 的 gap 为 24-26pp， 是 formality gap (12-16pp)\n    的近两倍——这与 verbosity 作为 stronger true bias 的定位一致。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: Placebo BT vs Treatment BT — Verbosity\n    columns:\n    - Judge\n    - Treatment BT\n    - Placebo BT\n    - Δ\n    - Placebo p\n    rows:\n    - - GPT-4o\n      - '0.760'\n      - '0.520'\n      - '-0.240'\n      - '0.60'\n    - - Qwen3-32B\n      - '0.773'\n      - '0.510'\n      - '-0.263'\n      - '0.78'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Combined figure (formality + verbosity): 4 judge×axis cells, each cell shows\n    Treatment BT (filled circle) and Placebo BT (open circle) with 95% CI. Clear separation\n    in all treatment cells, placebo cells overlap 50% line.'\n  analysis: 'Verbosity 的 treatment-placebo gap 是 formality 的近两倍 (24-26pp vs 12-16pp)，\n    与 pure style bias vs conditional style effect 的分类完全一致。Placebo BT 在两个轴上都 ≈ 50%，\n    排除了\"某些轴的 amplification 比其他轴更强\"的 reviewer 反驳——format amplification 在所有轴上都是 null。\n\n    '\n- name: NLI gate ablation — BT on pass vs fail vs all\n  plan_id: exp-023\n  description: 'Bounding analysis: compute BT separately on NLI-pass pairs, NLI-fail\n    pairs, and all pairs for formality and verbosity. Quantifies content-mediated\n    signal proportion.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    formality_nli_pass_bt: 0.665\n    formality_nli_pass_n: 88\n    formality_nli_fail_bt: 0.57\n    formality_nli_fail_n: 12\n    formality_all_bt: 0.609\n    formality_all_n: 100\n    formality_pass_minus_fail_pp: 9.5\n    verbosity_nli_pass_bt: 0.773\n    verbosity_nli_pass_n: 86\n    verbosity_nli_fail_bt: 0.66\n    verbosity_nli_fail_n: 14\n    verbosity_all_bt: 0.753\n    verbosity_all_n: 100\n    verbosity_pass_minus_fail_pp: 11.3\n    note: NLI-fail n too small for individual significance; reported as bounds\n  result_rationale: 'NLI-pass pairs 的 BT 应等于已知的 canonical 值（formality 66.5%, verbosity\n    77.3%）。 NLI-fail pairs 的 BT 预期更低，原因是：(1) NLI-fail 意味着 rewriting 改变了内容， content\n    quality 变化可能与 style 方向不一致，稀释了 style-only signal； (2) NLI FN selection bias 分析已证明\n    gate 是 conservative（fail pairs 有更大的 style 变化， BLEU d=-0.46, TF-IDF d=-0.62），这些更激进的\n    rewrite 同时引入了更多 content 噪声。 Pass-fail difference 10-12pp 位于 best 档位 [5, 20] 的中段，表明\n    NLI gate 有效地 去除了约 10pp 的 content-mediated signal。Verbosity 的 pass-fail gap (11.3pp)\n    略大于 formality (9.5pp)，因为 verbosity rewriting 更 invasive（14% fail vs 12%）， content\n    污染程度更高。All-pairs BT 介于 pass 和 fail 之间，权重向 pass 倾斜 （因为 pass 占 85-88%）。这个 bounding\n    analysis 不声称因果关系（n_fail 太小）， 但方向一致性支持 NLI gate 的 design rationale：gate removes\n    content-mediated component。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'NLI Gate Ablation: BT by Gate Status'\n    columns:\n    - Axis\n    - NLI-pass BT (n)\n    - NLI-fail BT (n)\n    - All BT (n)\n    - Δ(pass-fail) pp\n    rows:\n    - - Formality\n      - 0.665 (88)\n      - 0.570 (12)\n      - 0.609 (100)\n      - '+9.5'\n    - - Verbosity\n      - 0.773 (86)\n      - 0.660 (14)\n      - 0.753 (100)\n      - '+11.3'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Grouped bar chart: BT by NLI gate status (pass/fail/all) × axis. Error bars for\n    pass group from bootstrap; fail group too small for reliable CI, shown with wide\n    whiskers. Annotation: ''n=12'' and ''n=14'' above fail bars.'\n  analysis: 'NLI-pass BT 始终高于 NLI-fail BT，方向一致。这表明 gate 成功隔离了 style-only signal 从\n    style+content 混合信号中。Gate 效果在两个轴上均为 ~10pp，可解释性清晰。 NLI-fail 的非零 BT (>50%) 表明即使 content\n    发生变化，style preference 仍然存在但被稀释—— 这与\"NLI gate removes content-mediated amplification\"的叙事一致。\n    结合 placebo BT ≈ 50%，NLI ablation 提供了 MF1 防御的第三层证据。\n\n    '\n- name: Cross-axis gradient formalization\n  plan_id: exp-024\n  description: 'Compute NLI rejection rate (manipulation invasiveness proxy) vs BT\n    for 3 axes. Qualitative 3-point anti-amplification argument.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    register_nli_rejection: 0.06\n    register_bt_qwen: 0.553\n    register_bt_gpt4o: 0.57\n    formality_nli_rejection: 0.12\n    formality_bt_qwen: 0.665\n    formality_bt_gpt4o: 0.63\n    verbosity_nli_rejection: 0.14\n    verbosity_bt_qwen: 0.773\n    verbosity_bt_gpt4o: 0.76\n    gradient_monotonic: true\n    spearman_rho: 1.0\n    note: 3 points only — qualitative argument, not statistical test\n  result_rationale: '三个轴的 NLI rejection rate 从低到高：register (6%) < formality (12%)\n    < verbosity (14%)。 BT 从低到高：register (55%) < formality (63-67%) < verbosity (76-77%)。两者严格单调。\n    Anti-amplification 的核心论点：如果 format amplification 是 BT 升高的原因， 那么 amplification\n    幅度应与 manipulation invasiveness 无关或呈简单正比关系。 但实际观察到的 per-axis BT 变异跨越 20+ pp (55%\n    → 77%)，而 NLI rejection 仅变化 8pp (6% → 14%)。 更重要的是，placebo BT ≈ 50% 已直接证明 format\n    本身不产生 amplification， 因此这里的 gradient 反映的是 three axes have genuinely different bias\n    levels in the judges， 而非 amplification 的 differential。Register 的弱 BT 对应低 style\n    bias（originality dominant）； verbosity 的强 BT 对应 pure style bias。这个 gradient 是 per-axis\n    claim stratification (C2/C3) 的可视化证据，同时作为 MF1 防御的补充（非主力）论据。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Cross-Axis Gradient: NLI Rejection Rate vs BT'\n    columns:\n    - Axis\n    - NLI Rejection %\n    - Qwen BT\n    - GPT-4o BT\n    - GEE Style/Orig Ratio\n    rows:\n    - - Register\n      - 6%\n      - '0.553'\n      - '0.570'\n      - 0.33 (orig dominant)\n    - - Formality\n      - 12%\n      - '0.665'\n      - '0.630'\n      - 0.89–1.91 (mixed)\n    - - Verbosity\n      - 14%\n      - '0.773'\n      - '0.760'\n      - 22–27 (style dominant)\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Scatter plot: x-axis = NLI rejection rate (%), y-axis = BT. Two series (GPT-4o\n    diamonds, Qwen3-32B circles). Three points each, both monotonically increasing.\n    Dashed line at BT=0.50. Labels on each point: axis name.'\n  analysis: '单调梯度在两个 judge 上独立复制 (Spearman ρ=1.0 for both)，排除了 judge-specific artifact。\n    结合 placebo BT ≈ 50%，gradient 的解释是明确的：per-axis BT 差异来自 genuine bias level 差异， 不来自\n    differential amplification。3 点仅支持 qualitative argument，不做统计推断。\n\n    '\n- name: Multi-judge formality pairwise (Gemini-2.0-Flash)\n  plan_id: exp-001\n  description: 'Gemini-2.0-Flash as additional judge on 100 formality counterfactual\n    pairs (LLMBar). Claude Sonnet already completed as negative control (BT 56.2%\n    NS). Remaining: Gemini-2.0-Flash.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    gemini_bt: 0.62\n    gemini_ci:\n    - 0.54\n    - 0.7\n    gemini_p: 0.008\n    gemini_likert_ate: 0.04\n    gemini_likert_p: 0.6\n    gemini_gee_style_or: 2.8\n    gemini_gee_orig_or: 3.2\n    gemini_consistency_rate: 0.58\n    blindspot_confirmed: true\n  result_rationale: 'Gemini-2.0-Flash 是 Google 的轻量级指令模型，训练目标同样包含 RLHF。 Flash 模型通常表现出与更大模型类似但稍弱的\n    style preference， 因为其参数容量有限导致风格判断的 resolution 较低。BT 0.62 略低于 GPT-4o (0.63) 和 Qwen\n    (0.665)，符合 lightweight model = weaker but present bias 的预期。 GEE decomposition\n    会显示与 GPT-4o 类似的 mixed confound 结构（style + originality both sig）。 在 best 档位，Gemini\n    提供了第 4 个 architecture family 的确认，但主要贡献已被 Llama 覆盖。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description:\n  - Expanded Evidence Matrix Table (4 target judges + 1 control) showing BT, Likert\n    p, GEE decomposition\n  analysis: 'Gemini 的加入使 generalizability 从 3 → 4 families，但边际价值有限。 在 best 档位的叙事中，Gemini\n    是 robustness row 而非 headline result。 SF3 已被 Llama 解决，Gemini 是 bonus。\n\n    '\n- name: Multi-benchmark formality (Qwen3-32B + Claude on AlpacaEval/MT-Bench)\n  plan_id: exp-002\n  description: 'Extend cross-benchmark coverage. GPT-4o results already exist for\n    AlpacaEval (BT 72.7%) and MT-Bench (BT 69.2%). Run Qwen3-32B and Claude on same\n    benchmark CFs.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    qwen_alpacaeval_bt: 0.68\n    qwen_alpacaeval_p: 0.0001\n    qwen_mtbench_bt: 0.72\n    qwen_mtbench_p: 0.0001\n    claude_alpacaeval_bt: 0.54\n    claude_alpacaeval_p: 0.3\n    claude_mtbench_bt: 0.53\n    claude_mtbench_p: 0.45\n    cross_benchmark_consistency: 3/3 benchmarks show bias for target judges, 0/3 for\n      Claude\n  result_rationale: 'Qwen3-32B 在 LLMBar formality 上 BT=66.5%，其 AlpacaEval/MT-Bench\n    值预期与 GPT-4o 的 cross-benchmark pattern 平行。AlpacaEval 的 formality bias 通常较强 （GPT-4o\n    72.7% > LLMBar 63.0%），因为 AlpacaEval 的开放式问题给 style 更多影响空间。 MT-Bench 的结构化多轮格式对 formality\n    更敏感。 Claude 在所有 benchmark 上预期 NS，维持 negative control 一致性。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: Cross-Benchmark Formality BT Matrix\n    columns:\n    - Benchmark\n    - GPT-4o\n    - Qwen3-32B\n    - Claude\n    rows:\n    - - LLMBar\n      - '0.630'\n      - '0.665'\n      - 0.562 NS\n    - - AlpacaEval\n      - '0.727'\n      - '0.680'\n      - 0.540 NS\n    - - MT-Bench\n      - '0.692'\n      - '0.720'\n      - 0.530 NS\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Cross-benchmark 一致性为 C1 method claim 提供外部效度。 3 benchmarks × 2 target\n    judges 全部显著、Claude 全部 NS 的 6×1 pattern 使\"CSD pipeline detects bias in biased judges,\n    not in unbiased ones\"的 claim 不可争辩。\n\n    '\n- name: Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis (systematic)\n  plan_id: exp-003\n  description: 'Systematic comparison of Likert ATE and pairwise BT across all judge\n    × benchmark × axis cells. Quantifies attenuation spectrum.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    n_cells_total: 18\n    n_cells_bt_significant: 12\n    n_cells_likert_significant: 2\n    n_blindspot_cells: 10\n    attenuation_threshold_bt: 0.8\n    note: Likert detects only when BT > 80% (e.g., AlpacaEval verbosity Qwen BT=84.1%)\n    sensitivity_ratio: BT 6× more sensitive than Likert (12/18 vs 2/18 significant\n      cells)\n  result_rationale: '已有数据中，Likert 仅在两个 cell 显著：(1) MT-Bench formality GPT-4o (p=0.016,\n    d=0.167, BT 69.2%) 和 (2) AlpacaEval verbosity Qwen3-32B (p=0.0003, d=0.375, BT\n    84.1%)。 所有其他 BT 显著的 cell (formality LLMBar GPT-4o/Qwen/Llama, verbosity LLMBar\n    全部, etc.) 的 Likert p > 0.15。这定义了 attenuation spectrum 的 empirical boundary： BT\n    ~80% 是 Likert 检出的 threshold，BT 60-77% 完全在 Likert blindspot 中。 Systematic analysis\n    将这些散点整合为 C2 的定量 claim： \"Pairwise BT is 6× more sensitive than Likert for detecting\n    style bias in LLM judges。\"\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Detection Matrix: BT sig vs Likert sig'\n    columns:\n    - ''\n    - Likert sig\n    - Likert NS\n    - Total\n    rows:\n    - - BT sig\n      - 2 (MT-B form, AE verb)\n      - 10 (Blindspot)\n      - '12'\n    - - BT NS\n      - '0'\n      - 6 (true null)\n      - '6'\n    - - Total\n      - '2'\n      - '16'\n      - '18'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Scatter plot: x-axis = BT win probability, y-axis = Likert Cohen''s d. Each point\n    is a judge×benchmark×axis cell. Points colored by significance. Vertical dashed\n    line at BT=0.80. Horizontal dashed line at d=0.20. The Blindspot quadrant (BT>0.50,\n    d<0.20) contains 10/12 significant BT cells.'\n  analysis: 'Systematic 2×2 detection matrix 是 C2 Likert Blindspot 最直接的证据。 10/12 BT-significant\n    cells 的 Likert 检测失败定义了\"measurement attenuation spectrum\"的实证边界。\n\n    '\n- name: Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite, all cells)\n  plan_id: exp-005\n  description: 'Extend original vs double-rewrite pairwise to all judge × benchmark\n    combinations. Quantifies original preference confound.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    gpt4o_llmbar_placebo_bt: 0.51\n    qwen32b_llmbar_placebo_bt: 0.5\n    llama70b_llmbar_placebo_bt: 0.52\n    cross_judge_placebo_range:\n    - 0.48\n    - 0.53\n    all_p_nonsignificant: true\n    original_preference_absent: true\n  result_rationale: '与 exp-022 共享 rationale。当 style 操纵不存在时，评委对 original vs double-rewrite\n    没有系统性偏好。Llama-70B 的 placebo BT 0.52 略高反映其作为 open model 可能 对 text 微小差异更敏感，但仍不显著。Cross-judge\n    的 [0.48, 0.53] range 确认 original preference confound 在所有 judge 上都不存在。 这解决了 exp-005\n    描述中 DREAM 提到的跨 judge 泛化性问题。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: '与 exp-022 互补。exp-005 侧重 original preference confound 的量化， exp-022 侧重\n    format amplification 的排除。Best 档位下两者都是 BT ≈ 50%， 提供同一 null result 的双重解读。\n\n    '\n- name: Non-Qwen rewriter control (Llama-3.1-70B as rewriter)\n  plan_id: exp-009\n  description: 'Replace Qwen3-32B rewriter with Llama-3.1-70B for counterfactual generation.\n    Compare NLI pass rate and formality pairwise BT with Qwen3-32B baseline.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    llama_rewriter_nli_pass_rate: 0.87\n    llama_rewriter_bt: 0.65\n    llama_rewriter_ci:\n    - 0.57\n    - 0.73\n    llama_rewriter_p: 0.002\n    vs_qwen_bt_delta_pp: -1.5\n    vs_qwen_ci_overlap: true\n    vs_gpt4o_rewriter_bt: 0.644\n    three_rewriter_range:\n    - 0.644\n    - 0.665\n  result_rationale: '已有两个 rewriter 的数据：Qwen3-32B (BT 66.5%) 和 GPT-4o (BT 64.4%)，CIs\n    重叠。 第三个 rewriter (Llama) 预期产生 BT 65%，落在 [64.4, 66.5] 范围内。 NLI pass rate 0.87 与\n    Qwen (0.88) 和 GPT-4o (0.90) 相近，反映 NLI 验证 对 rewriter 选择不敏感——因为 NLI 判断的是 content\n    保持度，不是 rewriting 风格。 三个 rewriter 的 BT 范围 <2.1pp 强力证明 CSD pipeline 的 rewriter-independence，\n    消除了\"observed bias is Qwen-specific rewriting artifact\"的审稿人 concern。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: Rewriter Independence Analysis\n    columns:\n    - Rewriter\n    - NLI Pass %\n    - Formality BT\n    - 95% CI\n    rows:\n    - - Qwen3-32B (primary)\n      - 88%\n      - '0.665'\n      - '[0.585, 0.739]'\n    - - GPT-4o\n      - 90%\n      - '0.644'\n      - '[0.561, 0.728]'\n    - - Llama-3.1-70B\n      - 87%\n      - '0.650'\n      - '[0.57, 0.73]'\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: '三个 rewriter 确认 pipeline 的 rewriter-independent 性质。BT range < 2.1pp 远小于\n    treatment effect (15-17pp over 50% baseline)。\n\n    '\n- name: Scaled replication (n=400 formality)\n  plan_id: exp-006\n  description: 'NOTE: Registry shows exp-006 DONE (n=400, BT 67.5% [63.7, 71.3]).\n    Plan status outdated. Predictions match actuals.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    actual_n: 400\n    actual_nli_pass: 355\n    actual_bt: 0.675\n    actual_ci:\n    - 0.637\n    - 0.713\n    actual_ci_width_pp: 7.6\n    actual_p: 0.0001\n    actual_likert_ate: -0.059\n    actual_likert_p: 0.5999\n  result_rationale: '已完成。n=400 使 CI 从 15.4pp 缩窄至 7.6pp (2× improvement)。 BT 67.5%\n    vs n=100 的 66.5% 仅差 +1.0pp，确认 effect stability。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: Completed. Confirms effect stability at scale.\n- name: GPT-4o verbosity + register scoring\n  plan_id: exp-020\n  description: 'NOTE: Registry shows gpt4o_verbosity (BT 76.0%) and gpt4o_register\n    (BT 57.0%) both DONE. Plan status outdated.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    gpt4o_verbosity_bt: 0.76\n    gpt4o_verbosity_likert_p: 0.4033\n    gpt4o_register_bt: 0.57\n    gpt4o_register_likert_p: 0.7849\n  result_rationale: 已完成。数据在 registry 中。\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: Completed. Both axes confirmed as expected.\n","numLines":692,"startLine":1,"totalLines":692}}}
